The search thread's lambda took the parameter p by reference, and StartThinkThread
returns at once: the thread then read p from a dead stack frame. GCC builds happened
to work; clang builds (the NDK's, AddressSanitizer: stack-use-after-return) searched
garbage and answered illegal moves (bestmove a1b1 from the start). Take p by value.

diff --git a/sources/src/rodent.h b/sources/src/rodent.h
index 30ccf22..3e100a0 100755
--- a/sources/src/rodent.h
+++ b/sources/src/rodent.h
@@ -981,7 +981,7 @@ class cEngine {
     std::thread mWorker;
     void StartThinkThread(POS *p) {
         mDpCompleted = 0;
-        mWorker = std::thread([&] { Think(p); });
+        mWorker = std::thread([this, p] { Think(p); });
     }
 
     ~cEngine() { WaitThinkThread(); };  // should fix crash on windows on console closing
